    rationale: "CORRECT (A) — “Full-thickness tearing and breach of the skin surface”. A contusion is by definition a closed injury: blunt force damages small vessels and tissue beneath skin that stays intact, so blood leaks into the tissue and produces bruising, tenderness and swelling without any break in the surface. Full-thickness tearing and breach of the skin define an open wound, a laceration, which is a different injury class altogether. Why the other options fail: erythema and bruising over the injured area (B), tenderness on palpation (C) and subcutaneous oedema with swelling (D) are all genuine features of a contusion, which is why none of them is the answer to a question asking what is not.",
