    "correctChoiceId": "b",
    rationale: "CORRECT (B) — “Core body temperature regulation”. The hypothalamus holds the body’s thermostat and drives the responses that keep core temperature steady. Infarction there can leave the patient poikilothermic, so she takes on the temperature of the room, or hyperthermic or hypothermic without an infection. Why the other options fail: coordination and balance are cerebellar (A); abstract reasoning and calculation belong to the frontal cortex (C); and visual processing happens in the occipital lobe (D).",
    strategy: "Neuroanatomy matching: Hypothalamus = Thermoregulation, water balance, hunger, and autonomic drive. Cerebellum = Balance.",
