    rationale: "Reactive arthritis (formerly Reiter's syndrome) is a seronegative autoimmune spondyloarthropathy triggered by genitourinary or gastrointestinal infection. It affects joints, urethra, and eyes, not lymphatic vessels. Elephantiasis, Hodgkin's disease, and splenomegaly directly involve the lymphoid system.",
