    correctChoiceId: "a",
    rationale: "Pyridostigmine inhibits acetylcholinesterase, leading to acetylcholine accumulation and potent stimulation of cholinergic muscarinic receptors. This powerfully accelerates smooth muscle contraction and peristalsis. In the presence of mechanical bowel or urinary obstruction, increased luminal pressure against a blockage can lead to bowel perforation or bladder rupture.",
