    rationale: "Non-sterile protective apparel (hair cap, protective eyewear, and surgical mask) must always be donned before performing the surgical hand scrub. If donned afterward, the scrubbed hands would contact non-sterile surfaces and skin, causing immediate microbial contamination. Following hand scrubbing and sterile drying, the scrub nurse dons the sterile gown, followed by sterile gloves using closed gloving technique.",
