    correctChoiceId: "b",
    rationale: "Human skin cannot be completely sterilized without causing severe chemical or thermal tissue necrosis. Preoperative skin antisepsis is designed to remove transient pathogenic microbes acquired from the environment and dramatically suppress resident microbial flora (such as Staphylococcus epidermidis) to levels that minimize surgical site infection risk.",
    strategy: "Recognize that living tissue can never be sterilized; skin preparation achieves antisepsis (transient eradication and resident reduction), not absolute sterility.",
