    correctChoiceId: "c",
    rationale: "Closed wound suction drains (such as Jackson-Pratt or Hemovac) evacuate blood, lymphatic fluid, and inflammatory exudate that accumulate within operative dead space. Fluid collection in dead space creates tissue tension, delays wound healing, and provides a rich culture medium for bacterial proliferation and abscess formation.",
    strategy: "Focus on the primary mechanical function of wound drains: removing fluid and exudate from dead space to prevent seroma and hematoma formation.",
