    rationale: "Serous drainage is clear to pale yellow, thin, and watery, composed primarily of serum (plasma) that leaks from capillaries during the normal inflammatory phase of wound healing. Purulent drainage is thick, opaque, yellow/green; sanguineous is bright red blood; and serosanguineous is thin, watery, and pink.",
