    rationale: "In adults, the spinal cord terminates as the conus medullaris at the lower border of L1 or upper L2. To avoid damaging the spinal cord, a lumbar puncture needle is safely inserted below this level, typically between L3-L4 or L4-L5, accessing the subarachnoid space containing the cauda equina suspended in CSF.",
