    correctChoiceId: "a",
    rationale: "Intact epidermis and dermis constitute the body's primary mechanical barrier against microbial invasion. A surgical incision breaks this anatomical barrier, providing a direct port of entry for external pathogens into warm, vascular subcutaneous tissues. Aseptic technique prevents introducing exogenous pathogens into the vulnerable wound bed.",
