    rationale: "The diagnostic goal is to obtain lower respiratory secretions, not saliva. Morning collection is ideal because mucus accumulates overnight. The client should rinse the mouth with sterile water (avoiding antiseptic mouthwash, which may kill the target bacteria), take several deep diaphragmatic breaths, and cough forcefully from deep in the lungs into a sterile container.",
